From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winex11: the X keyboard map's layouts are its group names (9153)

winex11 (8212, 8217, 9901) learnt which Windows layout the X keyboard map
is from the XKB rules names on the root window (_XKB_RULES_NAMES). Under
Xwayland -- how every Windows program on Stained Glass is shown -- the X
map is the compositor's keymap, compiled from its text: _XKB_RULES_NAMES
keeps the X server's defaults ("evdev", "pc105", "us") and the symbols are
"(unnamed)". So on a German, French or Swedish desktop the default HKL
(9901) said US English, the layout the person typed with was answered as
US for programs that loaded US English, and GetKeyboardLayoutName said
00000409. setxkbmap, which the gates used, does set the rules names, so
they did not see it.

The names the compiled map does keep are its groups' ("German", "English
(US)", "English (Dvorak)"), which are the descriptions of the XKB rules'
layouts and variants (evdev.xml) the symbols files give their groups. The
X map's layouts are now read from the group names, matched against the
rules' layout list; only when a group's name is not there are the rules
names read, as before. Every group is read (a session can have two layouts,
switched with the Windows logo key + Space), and the group the keyboard
types with now.

Gate test/kbdxwayland-gate.sh: an Xvfb given the keymap the way Xwayland is
(xkbcommon's keymap text, loaded with xkbcomp: rules names stay "us"), then
the default HKL, its name and its keys. Mutant SG_MUTANT_KBD_RULES_NAMES.
